properties sit inside the jar


takes application.properties file from the jar
put another file next to the previous one and it will overrides

@value-> features
1:provide the default value if the properties is values is not present
2:managing the list
3:managing map of values


#->treat value after as an expression
//db.username=ankit
@Configuration->used to create the beans for this class
@ConfigurationProperties("db")->db.username,db.password
instead to pulling the single single value @configuration annotation is used to
create the beans at once inject the beans the at once
it is a class level level annotation

when to use @value and and @configurationProperties annotation

if you want to fetch the single value from properties use @value properties

if the are multiple value and are used in the multiple places use
@configurationProperties with @autowired in the respective class

//another example
my:
servers:
	- dev.example.com
	- another.example.com

my.servers[0]=dev.example.com
my.servers[1]=another.example.com

@ConfigurationProperties(prefix="my")
public class Config {

	private List<String> servers = new ArrayList<String>();

	public List<String> getServers() {
		return this.servers;
	}
}

actuator->provies all the endpoints
expose all the endpoints - > management.endpoints.web.exposure.include=*

all the endpoints of actuator are not exposed because of the sensitive information

/actuator/config props

what are ways to save the configuration of your application
difference between properties file and yml
1:properties files->key=value pair
2:yml->key:value,it has nesting structures ,means common thing
can put at one place with indentation to avoid the repeated things

spring profile
if  no active profile set in that case all the set of configuration is
 belongs to by default profile will run by spring(default profile is always active )

syntax->application-<properties name>.extn(ex ->.yml,.properties)

use case ->you can create the spring profile for different env like local,
            dev,production->
            keep the common thing in the default one and the one change as per env keep
            them in their env

spring-cloud-config-server->used as config as service where multiple
microservices interact with each others ,, where config is store on source(git).
setting up spring cloud config server->achieved centralised,externalised and
consistent config server.

now after this multiple microservices can consume this configuration
from spring cloud  config server rather than local properties file by
creating spring cloud config client

client(suppose microservice ) in yml or properties file we
declare the spring.cloud.config.uri = http://localhost:8888 and
client pull the data from server and hardcoded data in yml
if present then it overrides it.

real time management (refreshing properties at the runtimes)



